.TH AGENT-HOOK-POST-EDIT 1 "2026-06-30" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-post-edit \- format edited files and validate edited configs through Sley
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-post-edit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-post-edit
reads an agent edit hook JSON payload from standard input and delegates changed
files to
.BR "sley hook format --stdin" ,
one batch per directory (with a per-file
.BR "sley hook format-file"
fallback for older Sley installs).
It then passes edited JSON, JSONC, JSON5, YAML, and TOML files to
.BR "sley hook lint --stdin"
and returns its findings (exit status 1) as agent context, bounded to the
first 40 lines, so schema errors surface at edit time even in configs no
commit checks.
Lint that cannot run is not reported.
Code files and all other lint and verification remain native commit-hook
responsibilities so human and agent commit workflows share the same
readiness path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Formatting completed, selected formatter failures were ignored after Sley
surfaced them, or no format target was selected.
Config lint findings do not change the exit status.
.TP
.B 2
The local install is missing required dependencies such as
.BR sley .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-pre-edit (1),
.BR sley (1)
